#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e461ec99-72eb-5b6b-9663-930b2859964e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-70x+70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330938} {:answer/id #uuid "604254a9-d1e2-57c0-ba5c-19829615bb29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}-50{x}^{2}+15x-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330939} {:answer/id #uuid "a64adb75-e3f1-5869-a825-83e9072b55f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{3}-50{x}^{2}+160x-160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330940} {:answer/id #uuid "312e751e-6ffe-5694-b08a-e30c67f79757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}^{3}+50{x}^{2}-15x+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330941} {:answer/id #uuid "91cbdccd-9634-5e88-8d58-01a57d8ca4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}^{3}+50{x}^{2}-160x+160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cbdccd-9634-5e88-8d58-01a57d8ca4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}^{3}+50{x}^{2}-160x+160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330942} :answer-field/id #uuid "54a37c3d-3952-5448-a0b3-ba6ad257b9a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f245d15-61bb-55e5-8528-9e0a762de9e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104462" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2,{x}_{2}={x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-5.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-5(x-2)(x-4)(x-4) \\\\  & =-5(x-2)(x-4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5(x-2)(x-4)(x-4) & =-5({x}^{2}-6x+8)(x-4) \\\\  & =-5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}+24x+8x-32) \\\\  & =-5({x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+32x-32) \\\\  & =-5{x}^{3}+50{x}^{2}-160x+160.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-5{x}^{3}+50{x}^{2}-160x+160.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330943 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6417af2b-0a47-592f-a594-dd629a924010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-21x+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330945} {:answer/id #uuid "ad448141-2f9c-5ab6-bfcf-d881d41f2395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+21x-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330946} {:answer/id #uuid "75f361eb-8acf-59c0-b177-33e0828f1cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+12x+18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330947} {:answer/id #uuid "99cd8e08-829a-5197-b288-8b76545856b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-21x+18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330948} {:answer/id #uuid "64a6683d-6c4f-5d36-ba30-c6bce9320788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-12x+22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99cd8e08-829a-5197-b288-8b76545856b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-21x+18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330948} :answer-field/id #uuid "252b2089-ffb7-5a9c-bacf-6a303fe970cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "128d5b26-43e1-5fcd-92bd-6969aedf5743" :question/math-academy-id "q-107539" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2,{x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-1(x-2)(x-3)(x-3) \\\\  & =-(x-2)(x-3)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x-2)(x-3)(x-3) & =-({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x-2) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+9x+12x-18) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+21x-18) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-21x+18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-21x+18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4d8838d-b303-5796-9a99-a76dd2698893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330952} {:answer/id #uuid "2a68f4a4-80cb-51c1-86d6-67601fd46675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d8838d-b303-5796-9a99-a76dd2698893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330952} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6bfdc1-e945-530e-86e5-2e1128d2ea21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2129c94b-c58d-5cb6-885f-9f1f8cebfdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2129c94b-c58d-5cb6-885f-9f1f8cebfdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330955} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00f29dd-42ae-516d-8b06-3c645742bdc3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ab7159-89db-5d91-a441-ddc926de3abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01ab7159-89db-5d91-a441-ddc926de3abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330957} :answer-field/id #uuid "98e1ec42-e406-56f4-b364-333be84357ba" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330956} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0323eed4-f2e8-5509-8919-1e77050931dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0323eed4-f2e8-5509-8919-1e77050931dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330959} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc46fa2e-79d0-562b-9cc8-adad5925d1d2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74c9a8e5-90b4-5268-8e9c-fc75ce69b404" :question/math-academy-id "q-316632" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-5,$ and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-4.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-5,$ and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-4(x-1)(x-(-5))(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =-4(x-1)(x+5)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4(x-1)(x+5)(x+2) & =-4({x}^{2}+4x-5)(x+2) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}+8x-5x-10) \\\\  & =-4({x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+3x-10) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}-12x+40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-4{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}-12x+40.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091f1f95-cef9-59b7-b7f9-1415cc9f5aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281857} {:answer/id #uuid "a541f8ff-b62d-5e66-a809-6d0299be5a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a541f8ff-b62d-5e66-a809-6d0299be5a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281858} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbdfc33-1e58-5242-8633-fda746b517e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2162cc48-61f0-5b5c-b430-32b49357ae0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2162cc48-61f0-5b5c-b430-32b49357ae0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281860} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c06412-5cae-5797-897d-bdb5c92ef289" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98939d20-aade-57be-a048-e1e7c4db19fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98939d20-aade-57be-a048-e1e7c4db19fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a2f2ed-5eff-58bb-bfec-92ee85b2fd15" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864} :answer-field/id #uuid "a70f3f5c-4515-5830-8325-e90e481a964b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a501a88c-c742-55d1-9428-8cda49f09e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-316649" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-(-5))(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+4x+20) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186330960 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d3d8e8c-7015-514a-83d5-689d89928164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d3d8e8c-7015-514a-83d5-689d89928164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330962} :answer-field/id #uuid "71eec172-b52c-5418-b4c8-f8193b53a4fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1907cff1-d30a-5b75-824e-0f4eeed40d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1907cff1-d30a-5b75-824e-0f4eeed40d3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330964} :answer-field/id #uuid "93924ffb-a290-5db3-a9aa-c4a3471f00b8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4be33203-eb3d-5b59-b741-3172d9bd920c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4be33203-eb3d-5b59-b741-3172d9bd920c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330966} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2d8b4fb-dea8-5833-96e3-217d302463fc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1df841d-233d-5571-b2fe-b548c0a2b431" :question/math-academy-id "q-316725" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-1-3\\text{i})-x(-1+3\\text{i})+(-1+3\\text{i})(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+10) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+10x-2{x}^{2}-4x-20) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+6x-20) & = \\\\ -2{x}^{3}-12x+40 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}-12x+40.$"}]}
